<title>HONG KONG: Shu resigns as Ka Wah Bank chairman.</title>
<headline>Shu resigns as Ka Wah Bank chairman.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ka Wah Bank Ltd said on Friday Shu Tse Wong would resign as chairman and Kwok Viem had been appointed to replace him with effect from July 1.</p>
<p>Shu, who will resign effective June 30 due to health reasons, was invited to maintain his directorship in the bank, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Ka Wah said Kwok joined the bank earlier this month as a director and has a broad range of experience in international banking.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
